From: RNSBox <rnsbox@localhost>
Date: Wed, 21 Oct 2026 22:40:00 +0300
Subject: [PATCH] textui: use the in-process log view on all platforms

urwid.Terminal runs tail(1) on a private PTY for the Log tab. Tearing that
vterm down while switching tabs can raise from os.read() and terminate the
whole TUI (observed on the SG2000 mainline board), and the extra process,
PTY and continuous redraw are costly on small routers. The in-process
last-N-lines view is already used on win32; use it everywhere.
---
 nomadnet/ui/textui/Log.py | 8 ++++----
 1 file changed, 4 insertions(+), 4 deletions(-)

--- a/nomadnet/ui/textui/Log.py
+++ b/nomadnet/ui/textui/Log.py
@@ -78,10 +78,10 @@
 
 
 def log_widget(app, platform=sys.platform):
-    if platform == "win32":
-        return LogTail(app)
-    else:
-        return LogTerminal(app)
+    # The in-process last-N view avoids urwid.Terminal's tail child: tearing
+    # that vterm down can crash the TUI when switching tabs, and a PTY +
+    # process per Log tab is costly on small routers.
+    return LogTail(app)
 
 # https://stackoverflow.com/a/34029605/3713120
 def _tail(f_name, n, offset=0):
